  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 128 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThe ridge will weaken over our area for the beginning of next\nweek. This will allow a weak frontal boundary to drag into the\narea on Monday and Tuesday. Some weak shortwaves aloft combined\nwith the surface boundary will allow isolated to scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms to develop. Have kept PoPs generally\nbelow 50% given the uncertainty in overall coverage. But we could\nsome locally heavy rainfall with the stronger storms particularly\non Monday. The ridge looks to expand westward into our area for \nthe middle to later part of the week which would result in mainly \ndry conditions with temperatures creeping back up into the mid \n90s. Temperatures on Tuesday and Wednesday will be a little cooler\ngiven more cloud cover and lower upper level heights.",
